meta {
  name: Rollback Deployment
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/deployments/{{deploymentId}}/rollback
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-Dev-User-ID: {{devUserId}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "app_version_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
  }
}

docs {
  Reverts a deployment to a specific prior AppVersion that passed audit
  by calling Orchestrator.Rollback with the target GitSHA. Returns 202
  Accepted; the state transitions asynchronously.

  Request body:
    to_revision   required UUID — must be a published or archived version
                  of the same app with an approved audit decision;
                  typically a prior version retrieved via
                  GET /api/v1/apps/:slug/versions

  NOTE: the body:json block above uses the key "app_version_id" — this
  is incorrect; the handler expects "to_revision". Update the key before
  sending this request.

  Validation / behaviour:
    1. Authentication required; parse deployment ID — 404 if not found.
    2. Caller must own the deployment or be PlatformAdmin — 403 otherwise.
    3. Deployment must not be in a terminal or deleting state.
    4. Deployment must have an orchestrator reference (last_argocd_app_name).
    5. to_revision must be a valid UUID, belong to the same app, be in published
       or archived state, and hold an approved audit decision.
    6. Orchestrator.Rollback called with target GitSHA; on failure, state set to failed_orchestrator.
    7. Row app_version_id updated to target; state set to applying.
    8. Write deployment.rolled_back to audit_logs.

  Responses:
    202 Accepted     — deployment row (state=applying, updated app_version_id)
    401 unauthorized — unauthenticated
    403 forbidden    — caller does not own the deployment
    404 not_found    — deployment or target version not found
    409 deployment_not_rollbackable — terminal or deleting state
    409 no_orchestrator_ref — deployment has no Argo CD reference
    422 validation   — bad UUID (invalid_uuid), wrong app (wrong_app),
                       version not published/archived or not audit-approved
                       (not_rollback_eligible)
    502 orchestrator_rollback_failed — orchestrator rejected the rollback
    503 orchestrator_not_configured — no orchestrator configured
}
